{
  "id": "skills",
  "version": "1.0",
  "asOf": "2026-01-01",
  "source": "The Skill Stacker's catalogue: twenty-six money skills, each tied to one of the seven Dungeons & Dividends classes (its lever) and the sub-stats it trains, with an effect either verified from the household's own facts or valued by a stated convention (BRIEF §7.1).",
  "confidence": "convention",
  "confidenceNote": "Every dollar figure here is a rule of thumb — a third off the dining line for cooking, $300 a year for a phone call — and says so in its source line. Effort figures are guesses at learning hours and daily practice minutes. Nothing here is measured.",
  "note": "kind: once (done when verified or marked), habit (logged daily; decays after decayDays missed), periodic (due every everyDays). effect: cents_per_year with a fixed cents or a formula in the events engine's expression language over the household context; risk effects are worth $0 by design. verify: a household fact that marks a once-skill done on load — field is an ownership row; present / equals / gteField / source. fooStep: the FOO step this belongs to (0 = any). level: 1 starter, 2 built, 3 practised. rules: the thresholds the engine reads, see there. D-090.",
  "rules": {
    "maxEquipped": 3,
    "windowDays": 30,
    "trialDays": 7,
    "habitDays": 21,
    "decayDays": 14,
    "lapseDays": 45,
    "nudgeMultiplier": 1.5,
    "minEffortHours": 0.25,
    "note": "maxEquipped: how many skills may sit in trial or practicing at once. A habit in trial becomes practicing at trialDays logged in the last windowDays and a habit at habitDays; a habit unlogged for the skill's own decayDays (else this default) falls back to practicing, and for lapseDays to available. nudgeMultiplier weights a skill that trains the lowest sub-stat in nextSkill. minEffortHours keeps return-on-effort finite for a skill with no stated effort."
  },
